I recommend you go with the spellslinger option.  Drop the metal armor
(except for the helmet perhaps) and replace it with non-metallic
counterparts.  Your AC won't be great, but it doesn't need to be if your
offense is good enough.  Liberate a robe if you can, and enchant it and your
hawaiian shirt, since you know you'll be keeping those.

Read all your spellbooks and start using them.  The two spells I get most
use out of as a tourist are identify and magic missile.  You can't advance
attack spells, but MM is a low level spell you can use early on and it only
gets better as you advance in level.

Daggers!  Seriously, don't underestimate them.  You're a tourist and can get
expert in daggers.  With your current strength and your ring of damage, an
expert with +7 daggers can do d4+16 per dagger (d5 if they're elven), and
can throw an average of two per turn.  Enchant a bunch of them and keep
10-15 in your quiver.

